answer/value "{22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434848} {:answer/id #uuid "58134ae4-42d3-52fa-8819-44f040d50e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{17}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434857} {:answer/id #uuid "8bdf038a-c572-5e99-bb81-010b2f268519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434874} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4970ce-e707-5070-9c09-72d2f72c7b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa4970ce-e707-5070-9c09-72d2f72c7b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434903} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b569db-566a-5790-a2c5-dd4d55aab5c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0760d1ac-bf3e-5fb3-a6d7-38383b9bd628" :question/math-academy-id "q-114128" :question/problem "![](images/12/12f9e7857f065a6fc457533c25adc4a00cdf4c325838a5865abd87d6fba90c4a.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BAE={160}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠DAE.$\n\nThe measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={160}^{∘}-{72}^{∘}-{63}^{∘}={25}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434836} {:answer/id #uuid "6b95ac2c-aed5-57a4-9c97-6dd27cda5944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{115}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434863} {:answer/id #uuid "771a247a-4f56-50b2-9664-5bd5a8a2d794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{95}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434868} {:answer/id #uuid "93f9fd6b-a694-5168-97ce-c9a7b439a6a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434876} {:answer/id #uuid "c3318d7a-e8df-5e9d-9938-8e9ff813fc7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434836} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f06001a-88ec-58d0-800a-3f395c862b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d2a2e76f-a9f4-53a0-a562-a0ade38c838f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114129" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a493b0c356b7088479ec6c80afff94eb5e39fd8b31d14b771076b9a9ab37ddc1.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠AOD={170}^{∘}$ and $m∠BOD={130}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠AOC.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠AOB$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AOD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BOD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠AOB={170}^{∘}-{130}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/12/12431bb2f66402469571c49ac5637376f89e54265748fa88b3a6450c14bd7bce.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠AOC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc3b37d-ee9e-561a-a603-10bed87792b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434838} {:answer/id #uuid "2014ad3b-af18-5cbf-9a7b-23ff3020c880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434845} {:answer/id #uuid "d537e57c-90be-562b-b367-68ce5cd0150e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434893} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fc0cfb-faea-58f7-904e-fa6bf4cd9de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{115}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434897} {:answer/id #uuid "f24c8cba-6ba0-5e2f-8d8b-2b6208716638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d537e57c-90be-562b-b367-68ce5cd0150e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434893} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9002bc1-78a6-565b-92e9-6d7ba056ce6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c50e45a5-1e9c-5cec-9df9-668befadb54f" :question/math-academy-id "q-114228" :question/problem "![](images/79/791eff28e744c432f7072ab4601e7105cff23e82db57b3d3c6aa5a82698458c4.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠POS={140}^{∘}$ and $m∠QOS={95}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠POR.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠POQ$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠POS)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠QOS).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠POQ={140}^{∘}-{95}^{∘}={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/94/94c67d7c4920f05641ee469cafceeb8b9dfe453ff19f80afd882a806afabbac5.png)\n\n   \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠POR:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠POR & =m∠POQ+m∠QOR \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={110}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d991493-389d-5e33-97a3-6f9039a36093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{115}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434854} {:answer/id #uuid "52965194-c33f-5a8e-88dd-e0042bd867a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434855} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc15f12-7fda-5cea-8b85-122795fc0188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{130}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434871} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bb23da-e4cf-565f-8cd2-7431922b50df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434883} {:answer/id #uuid "cd395771-6115-5298-bd67-844bd9701949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{125}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434891}] :an