\\\  & ={84}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060ae832-5075-56da-82fc-17a5809b5c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434835} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd9acdd-9fd8-534e-ae92-2b533b6f1435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{101}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434840} {:answer/id #uuid "48fdf3b5-2057-594f-84e9-26ee50f9ff83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434851} {:answer/id #uuid "75525703-7dca-57fe-a897-27f9b89f4f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{160}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434866} {:answer/id #uuid "cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434892} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d6b294-b913-5ee6-9387-4ce663001aab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a93b6132-98b2-52ec-8ca3-233cb9c50ee1" :question/math-academy-id "q-154876" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa5f7200cabc7aad7589c203d67dcbf81a6f632238369206e3845a89f25337c9.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BAE={120}^{∘}$ and $m∠BAD={80}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠CAE.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠DAE={120}^{∘}-{80}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/df/df3e0be0d89947829ede0fbd55b19cb8d0a13c77cf5ece6c25933254d7cce29f.png)\n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠CAE:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAE & =m∠CAD+m∠DAE \\\\  & ={60}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2a3aad-85e3-5fb4-829b-3d11835d963a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={75}^{∘}\\times {30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434844} {:answer/id #uuid "99e12a41-9481-5e9b-95dd-bd52b9d3c141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={75}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434877} {:answer/id #uuid "d5623039-c6f8-5229-a5e5-b42ca9bf909e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={75}^{∘}-{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434894} {:answer/id #uuid "ed189ece-e96b-5b2d-bb0f-eebcd71fa8c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={50}^{∘}+{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434900} {:answer/id #uuid "f8938f21-38c2-5de7-b34e-4354ae6a27e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={75}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8938f21-38c2-5de7-b34e-4354ae6a27e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={75}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434902} :answer-field/id #uuid "692760d2-82f6-5a6d-96f5-c4002798edfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71b1c542-5e69-591c-ba07-511c7d72ad49" :question/math-academy-id "q-154881" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fd4d965798c94af269ce527930ab888a882e01eb6737f4096d8fa36cbc496bfb.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠LON={75}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠MON.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠LOM$ and $∠MON$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OM}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠LON)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠LOM$ and $∠MON).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠MON$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠LON)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠LOM).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={75}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434856} :answer-field/id #uuid "957d23c2-2b79-5fed-9bde-ffd8c9acbe96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7d3aa87-356e-5bc2-8e85-8a227cbc986a" :question/math-academy-id "q-171821" :question/problem "![](images/89/89c36c6195b98d333a7fedaf2bd2fe72b8c7b334aa92b85a5cc0ba1fc1145897.png)\n\nSince the measure of $∠BAD$ in the diagram above is ${85}^{∘},$ the angle $x$ must be equal to{{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={85}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}={45}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e411cc0-fdb3-5fff-b845-77c0cb3bd379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434859} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed72a32-4f62-5d18-a45a-a67c35f83474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434860} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd6451b-a4cc-51ae-8e5e-c2320d85011d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434875} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7ddfb6-dfa1-5ed4-a381-456841eedea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434886} {:answer/id #uuid "e57c9abd-7f5b-5a91-97fb-8c10df7cbe52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{74}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ed72a32-4f62-5d18-a45a-a67c35f83474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434860} :answer-field/id #uuid "873bc689-a7e7-5413-a60b-d78d8191f318" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186109381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "915b9cd0-2037-5441-8562-105770a85a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-53140" :question/problem "![](images/85/850013d06343c35d1bc102be741e0061214bc66abf479167141da1ec4fd8c82f.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠AOC.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/cd/cd66b6b8c4e1a7a1deb68de79d842a21760df66d615721e933105361ea3f8af5.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠AOB$ and $∠BOC$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OB}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={32}^{∘}+{46}^{∘} \\\\  & ={78}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15e2a51e-6919-53ef-a340-c777e0278602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434843} {:answer/id #uuid "615b0b02-9899-5bec-bdae-86a42773e94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{92}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434862} {:answer/id #uuid "75752499-99ce-575d-8b4b-53fd798d44b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{102}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434867} {:answer/id #uuid "a96cf519-6e43-5bf9-a928-51b4545f543b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434878} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0ddb38-f16d-5cc8-bbfc-56d09910ac11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{99}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75752499-99ce-575d-8b4b-53fd798d44b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{102}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434867} :answer-field/id #uuid "45531b81-2329-5349-b43d-db17bbe04821" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eda042a4-74d7-5136-ac0b-5b4db6d8b88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-53141" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d378eeecb9b30f1f76fb54c4279e94b0f469a776c7d774067f100697df7c7c4c.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠BOD.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/17/17922d1ffef1dcd8bc798c8ffb8fe113a7e2e57cacc234641c84f59bbbcf6bbd.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OC}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOD & =m∠BOC+m∠COD \\\\  & ={52}^{∘}+{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ={102}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
